From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Arun Iyengar <aiyengar1990@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 5 Nov 2026 06:41:32 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 305/311] avcodec/cavsdec: add the plumbing for hwaccels

Let the decoder negotiate its pixel format with ff_get_format() at the
first sequence header, allocate the hwaccel private data of every
picture and, when a hwaccel is active, hand it the whole picture (from
the picture start code to the end of its last slice, as annex A keeps
start code prefixes out of the slice data) instead of decoding the
macroblock layer: start_frame() gets the picture, decode_slice() the
first slice start code onwards, so the hwaccel can tell where the slice
data begins. The sequence and picture header fields a stateless decoder
needs are parsed and kept: progressive_sequence, chroma_format,
sample_precision, frame_rate_code, top_field_first, repeat_first_field,
advanced_pred_mode_disable, the skip_mode_flag of a field coded I
picture, and the Guangdian (AVS+, GY/T 257.1) additions: bbv_delay
extension, no_forward_reference_flag, pb_field_enhanced_flag, the
weighting quantization parameters and aec_enable. Each reference keeps
its picture_structure and top_field_first, and the reference before
DPB[1] stays known by its distance and flags for the direct mode of B
pictures. The coded size is whole macroblocks (an even number of rows
when interlaced), horizontal_size and vertical_size the displayed part.

The Guangdian profile is accepted in the sequence header but, without a
hwaccel, refused as before; the software decoder's output is unchanged
(FATE cavs and the bunny and test card references).

Signed-off-by: Arun Iyengar <aiyengar1990@gmail.com>
---
